// c20_nested_named_functio.exsc
//
// Case c20. The mistake: a nested, named `functio` inside a function body
// (spec §8.6's peek: `functio IDENT` at statement-start is a nested named
// function -- `EXS-E0201`, no fix payload; otherwise it is a lambda
// expression statement).
//
// Review reported: `2:5 EXS-E0201`, no fix payload. Verdict: "good" --
// exactly what spec §8.6 *Peeks* mandates.
//
// Reconstruction: byte-faithful. Counting from the first byte of `publica`
// below, this file reproduces `2:5 EXS-E0201`, span on the inner
// `functio`, `fix: null` -- exactly as reported, and exactly one
// diagnostic (no cascade).

publica functio exterior() -> u64 {
    functio interior() -> u64 {
        redde 1;
    }
    redde interior();
}
